From e642bf4d5345c63226d8924b30b54ddc3ab17b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: leozhang <zwj8727@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:41:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 61/62] k27: piano-cpuidle=N: the idle loop's WFI becomes a
 PSCI CPU_SUSPEND vote (CPU, cluster, CPU subsystem) when it fits

Under Gunyah the HLOS's WFI is trapped and blocks the vCPU; the physical CPU then runs Gunyah's idle WFI, and Gunyah calls
the firmware's CPU_SUSPEND only when no vCPU of that CPU is active (a vCPU blocked in WFI is). A vCPU that calls CPU_SUSPEND
votes for a state instead. piano's states (its Linux DT, read as data), all extended-format retention states (StateType
clear, no local-timer-stop), so CPU_SUSPEND returns to the caller: ret 0x4 (cores 0-5 93/129/560 us, cores 6-7
172/130/686), cl5 0x01000054 (2150/1983/9144), ss3 0x0200c354 (2800/4400/10150).

- osfmk/arm64/piano_pm.c: piano-cpuidle=N (1 ret, 2 + cl5, 3 + ss3): at cpu_idle's WFI, the deepest level whose
  min-residency fits before cpu_data rtcPop and whose exit latency fits every hold (piano_cpuidle_latency_hold, for
  PianoTouch's DMA reads), else WFI. Domain states as Linux's cpuidle-psci-domain sends them (read as the specification):
  only from the last CPU of the cluster / of all, the domain's param in place of the CPU's, every CPU of the domain clear of
  its deadline; OS-initiated mode set at boot from the boot CPU when PSCI_FEATURES(CPU_SUSPEND) has bit 0
  (piano-cpuidle-pc=1 keeps platform-coordinated); a DENIED falls back to the CPU state at once; a state rejected as
  invalid 16 times in a row is disabled for that CPU. ss3 only with the LLCC island slice (SCID 12) reserved
  (0x7fffffff, no bonus ways; read through the broadcast base), or piano-llcc-island-ok=1.
- osfmk/arm64/piano_pm_policy.h: the decisions without hardware (state choice, wake sources and the wake calendar for
  0062, the Type-C address, the PSCI and LLCC verdicts), host-tested in UniXNU-piano tooling/k27/piano-pm.
- A probe at boot (also piano-pm-probe=1 alone): PSCI VERSION and FEATURES, the APPS RSC DRV2 id and solver bit, the
  AOP's RPMh sleep counters (aosd, cxsd, ddr at 0xc3f0048), the LLCC island slice. VERSION and FEATURES are SMC32 calls:
  their int32 in w0 is sign-extended, so NOT_SUPPORTED is -1 for the checks and the line (before 2026-11-12 the upper half
  of x0 read zero: "STAT_COUNT 4294967295", and a refused SET_SUSPEND_MODE would have tested as supported).
- Counters per CPU and state in counter ticks; "piano-cpuidle: cpuN state X entries .. residency ..%" and the RPMh line
  every piano-cpuidle-period s (60, 0 off); machdep.piano_cpuidle (string) and machdep.piano_cpuidle_level (read-write
  up to N).
- piano-cpuidle-pd=1 (experimental): ret requested as a power-down. Gunyah then warm-resets the vCPU at the reset vector:
  resume_idle_cpu -> start_cpu -> arm_init_idle_cpu, XNU's power-gated idle path, where piano_cpuidle_reset_resume()
  restores the GIC CPU interface ArmCpu set up once and reprograms the decrementer.
- Native only (the /psci conduit must be SMC); inert without the boot argument.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
